 and correlation among LLM benchmarks low-dimensional structure of benchmark scores\". The claim that suites \"are known to overlap in what they measure\" is cited only to the suites. This looks for empirical redundancy or correlation analyses beyond BenchBench and Observational Scaling Laws, which are already cited.\n\n### Gap 3: data-open-llm-leaderboard-context (medium)\n5. **benchmark_context:** \"Open LLM Leaderboard v2 evaluation of open language models\". This finds a source for one of the three sealed evaluation datasets.\n6. **benchmark_context:** \"IFEval instruction-following, BIG-Bench Hard, GPQA, MuSR, MMLU-Pro benchmark\". This finds sources for the six component benchmarks named in the protocol and appendix. BBH may already be partly covered by BIG-bench, and MATH Level 5 is not queried because the gap memo does not list it as a search topic. The retrieval step can resolve the individual papers.\n\n## Exclusions\nThe gap memo deliberately does not flag the rank-Gauss transform, kNN, numeric results, protocol facts, or the limitations and discussion text. No queries are planned for these. Queries must not name or hint at the prior published paper on this exact task.\n[semantic_scholar] fetching | [#-----------] | refs 1/25 (24 left) | candidates 1/10 | query 3/6\n[semantic_scholar] fetching | [#-----------] | refs 2/25 (23 left) | candidates 2/10 | query 3/6\n[semantic_scholar] fetching | [#-----------] | refs 3/25 (22 left) | candidates 3/10 | query 3/6\n[semantic_scholar] fetching | [##----------] | refs 4/25 (21 left) | candidates 4/10 | query 3/6\n[semantic_scholar] fetching | [##----------] | refs 5/25 (20 left) | candidates 5/10 | query 3/6\n[semantic_scholar] fetching | [###---------] | refs 6/25 (19 left) | candidates 6/10 | query 3/6\n[semantic_scholar] fetching | [###---------] | refs 7/25 (18 left) | candidates 7/10 | query 3/6\n[semantic_scholar] fetching | [####--------] | refs 8/25 (17 left) | candidates 8/10 | query 3/6\n[semantic_schola